          "name": "Is a brushless drill worth it for a homeowner?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For a main drill that will see decks, fences, hole saws and remodeling, yes; brushless typically gives more runtime per charge, holds speed under load and has no brushes to wear out. For light jobs like hanging pictures and assembling furniture, a brushed drill does the work for less money. Many homeowners own one of each."
