            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "On many brushed tools the carbon brushes are a wear part that a service center can replace, but on budget cordless tools the repair often costs close to a new bare tool. For a homeowner's drill, the brushes usually outlast the battery and the chuck under occasional use. If a brushed drill sparks heavily or loses power, check it under the 3-year warranty first."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do Ryobi 40V batteries fit ONE+ tools?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
